{"mask_iou": "Mask IoU is a metric for evaluating object detection and image segmentation models by measuring the overlap between predicted and ground truth object masks. It calculates the intersection over union (IoU) of the masks, providing a quantitative measure of alignment. This metric is crucial for assessing segmentation accuracy, is scale-invariant, and is often used with other metrics like Average Precision and Panoptic Quality. However, it may have a bias toward large objects and could over-penalize errors in small objects.|Here is another description: Mask IoU, or Intersection over Union for masks, is a metric that measures the overlap between the predicted object mask and the ground truth mask. It is used to evaluate the accuracy of instance segmentation models, with higher IoU values indicating better alignment between predicted and actual object boundaries."},
