{"boundary_based_segmentation_measures__estimate__contour_alignment_between_predicted_and_ground_truth_masks": "The predicate \"estimate\" in this context refers to the process by which boundary-based segmentation measures quantify the degree of alignment between the contours of predicted segmentation masks and those of ground truth masks. This estimation is crucial for evaluating the accuracy and effectiveness of the segmentation algorithm."},
{"contour_alignment_between_predicted_and_ground_truth_masks": "Contour alignment between predicted and ground truth masks represents the degree to which the boundaries of the segmentation results match the actual boundaries of the objects in the image. This alignment is a critical factor in determining the precision and reliability of the segmentation process."},
{"boundary_based_segmentation_measures__evaluate__pixels_that_lie_directly_on_the_masks_contours_or_in_their_close_proximity": "The predicate \"evaluate\" in this context refers to the process of assessing or judging the effectiveness and accuracy of boundary-based segmentation measures in determining how well the predicted segmentation contours align with the ground truth contours."},
{"pixels_that_lie_directly_on_the_masks_contours_or_in_their_close_proximity": "The object \"pixels that lie directly on the masks\u2019 contours or in their close proximity\" refers to the specific set of pixels in an image that are either exactly on the boundary of a segmentation mask or very near to it. These pixels are the focus of boundary-based segmentation measures when evaluating segmentation quality.|Here is another description: The object \"pixels that lie directly on the masks\u2019 contours or in their close proximity\" refers to the specific subset of pixels in an image that are either on the boundary of the segmentation masks or very close to these boundaries. These pixels are particularly important in boundary-based segmentation measures, which focus on evaluating the alignment of predicted mask contours with the ground truth contours."},
{"mask_based_measures": "Mask-based measures are a type of evaluation metric used in image segmentation tasks to assess the quality of segmentation results. They focus on comparing the entire predicted mask with the ground truth mask, rather than just the contours."},
{"mask_based_measures__evaluate__pixels_that_lie_directly_on_the_masks_contours_or_in_their_close_proximity": "The predicate \"evaluate\" in this context refers to the process of assessing or measuring the quality or accuracy of segmentation results using specific metrics. It involves comparing the predicted segmentation masks with the ground truth masks to determine how well the segmentation algorithm performs."},
