{"errors_of_different_magnitudes": "Errors of different magnitudes refer to discrepancies or inaccuracies that vary in size or severity. In the context of mask consistency measures, these errors are introduced to test how sensitive and responsive the measures are to different levels of error, helping to assess their robustness and effectiveness."},
{"we__observe_and_interpret__these_curves": "The predicate \"observe and interpret\" describes the actions taken by the subject to analyze the data. This involves looking at the data (observing) and making sense of it (interpreting) to understand the behavior of the measures."},
