{"that_simulated_errors_may_not_fully_represent_errors_created_by_real_models": "The object, \"that simulated errors may not fully represent errors created by real models,\" describes the nature of the limitation, highlighting that the simulated errors might not accurately or completely reflect the errors produced by actual segmentation models, thus potentially affecting the robustness and generalizability of the analysis."},
{"we__aim_to_counteract_this_limitation__by_using_a_diverse_set_of_error_types": "The predicate \"aim to counteract this limitation\" describes the researchers' goal to address a specific drawback in their methodology. This involves taking deliberate steps to enhance the representativeness and effectiveness of their error simulation approach."},
