{"dilation_and_erosion_of_the_mask": "Dilation and erosion of the mask are specific morphological operations in image processing. Dilation expands the boundaries of the mask, while erosion contracts them, both of which can lead to scale errors if not properly controlled."},
{"boundary_localization_error__involves__adding_random_gaussian_noise_to_each_vertex_in_polygons": "The predicate \"involves\" indicates that boundary localization error is characterized by or includes the process of adding random Gaussian noise to each vertex in polygons, which distorts the boundary representation."},
{"adding_random_gaussian_noise_to_each_vertex_in_polygons": "Adding random Gaussian noise to each vertex in polygons is a method used to simulate boundary localization error in image segmentation. This process introduces variability and inaccuracies in the boundary representation by perturbing the vertices of the polygon that outlines the segmented object."},
