{"shifting_masks": "Shifting masks is a method used to simulate object localization error in image segmentation. It involves moving the predicted object mask away from its correct position relative to the ground truth mask, thereby creating a discrepancy that represents the localization error."},
{"boundary_approximation_error": "Boundary approximation error is a type of error that occurs in the process of approximating the boundary of an object, often resulting in inaccuracies in the representation of the object's shape."},
