{"a_different_score": "A numerical value that differs when the prediction and ground truth masks are swapped, indicating a change in the evaluation metric due to the asymmetry of the Trimap IoU computation."},
{"asymmetry": "Asymmetry in this context refers to the lack of symmetry in the evaluation metric, specifically Trimap IoU, when comparing predictions to ground truth masks. It highlights the unequal treatment of predictions that are larger or smaller than the ground truth."},
{"asymmetry__favors__predictions_that_are_larger_than_ground_truth_masks": "The term 'favors' indicates a bias or preference in the evaluation metric towards certain types of predictions. In this case, it suggests that the metric tends to give better scores to predictions that exhibit a particular characteristic, which is being larger than the ground truth masks."},
{"predictions_that_are_larger_than_ground_truth_masks": "Predictions that are larger than ground truth masks are those where the predicted area exceeds the actual area defined by the ground truth. These types of predictions are preferred by the Trimap IoU metric due to its asymmetry, as it results in higher scores compared to predictions that are smaller than the ground truth."},
{"figure_4b": "Figure 4b is a visual representation or graph that illustrates a specific concept or data related to the asymmetry in Trimap IoU measurements."},
