{"large_relative_to_small_objects": "The phrase \"large relative to small objects\" describes a situation where the threshold _d_ is significantly larger in comparison to the size of small objects, which can affect the evaluation metrics like F-measure."},
{"f_measure__may_award__significant_errors_a_perfect_score": "The predicate \"may award\" indicates that under certain conditions, the F-measure can assign a perfect score to results that contain significant errors. This suggests a potential limitation in the metric's ability to accurately reflect the quality of the predictions."},
{"significant_errors_a_perfect_score": "Significant errors receiving a perfect score refers to instances where the F-measure, due to its design and the chosen distance threshold, incorrectly evaluates flawed predictions as flawless. This can occur when the threshold is large relative to the size of small objects, leading to an overestimation of performance."},
