{"figure_5__illustrates__boundary_iou_computation": "The predicate 'illustrates' indicates that Figure 5 serves as a visual aid to explain or clarify the concept of Boundary IoU computation. It shows the process and components involved in calculating this metric, making the abstract concept more tangible and easier to understand."},
{"boundary_iou_computation": "Boundary IoU computation refers to the process of calculating the Intersection over Union (IoU) specifically for the boundary regions of segmentation masks. This metric is used to evaluate how well the predicted boundaries of objects in an image match the ground truth boundaries, providing a measure of segmentation accuracy that focuses on the edges of objects."},
{"ground_truth_and_prediction_masks": "Ground truth and prediction masks refer to the actual and estimated segmentations of an image, respectively. These masks are crucial for evaluating the performance of segmentation algorithms by comparing the predicted segmentations against the true segmentations."},
{"ground_truth_and_prediction_masks__are_shown_in__figure_5_top": "The phrase \"are shown in\" indicates that the ground truth and prediction masks are visually presented or displayed within a specific section of the document or figure. This presentation allows for a direct comparison and evaluation of the segmentation results."},
{"figure_5_top": "Figure 5 (top) is a specific part of the document where the ground truth and prediction masks are illustrated. This figure is used to visually demonstrate the segmentation results and to highlight the regions within a certain distance from the contours, which are important for computing segmentation consistency measures like Boundary IoU."},
{"mask_pixels": "Mask pixels refer to the individual pixels that make up a mask in image segmentation tasks. These pixels are specifically identified and highlighted in the context of evaluating segmentation accuracy."},
{"mask_pixels__are_within_distance__d_from_the_contours": "The phrase \"are within distance\" describes a spatial relationship where certain pixels are located at a specified distance from a reference point or feature, in this case, the contours of an object in an image."},
{"d_from_the_contours": "The object \"d from the contours\" specifies a distance measure, denoted as 'd', from the edges or boundaries (contours) of objects within an image. This distance is used to determine which pixels are considered in the evaluation of segmentation performance."},
{"boundary_iou_segmentation_consistency_measures": "Boundary IoU segmentation consistency measures are a method used to evaluate the consistency of segmentation results by focusing on the boundaries of segmented regions."},
{"boundary_iou_segmentation_consistency_measures__computes__the_intersection_over_union_between_the_highlighted_regions": "The predicate \"computes\" indicates the action performed by the Boundary IoU segmentation consistency measures, which is to calculate a specific metric."},
{"the_intersection_over_union_between_the_highlighted_regions": "The intersection-over-union between the highlighted regions refers to the ratio of the overlapping area between two sets of highlighted pixels (those within a certain distance from the contours of ground truth and prediction masks) to the area of their union, serving as a measure of segmentation accuracy."},
{"boundary_iou__is__0_73": "The term 'is' in this context signifies the value or result obtained from the computation of the Boundary IoU metric, indicating the degree of overlap between the boundary regions of the ground truth and predicted masks."},
{"0_73": "The value 0.73 represents the computed Boundary IoU, which is a quantitative measure of the intersection over union (IoU) between the highlighted boundary regions of the ground truth and prediction masks, reflecting a moderate level of segmentation consistency."},
{"mask_iou__is__0_91": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the value or measurement of the Mask IoU, indicating the degree of overlap between the ground truth and predicted masks."},
