{"a_random_confidence_score": "A random confidence score is a numerical value assigned to each bounding box to indicate the model's confidence in the correctness of the segmentation. This score is randomly assigned in the described context to isolate segmentation quality from other errors."},
{"detectron2": "Detectron2 is a state-of-the-art object detection framework developed by Facebook AI Research. It is widely used for various computer vision tasks, including object detection, instance segmentation, and keypoint detection.|Here is another description: Detectron2 is an advanced software framework for object detection, segmentation, and other computer vision tasks. It was developed by Facebook AI Research to provide a modular and scalable platform for researchers and developers.|Here is another description: Detectron2 is a software framework developed for object detection and segmentation tasks in computer vision. It is designed to be modular and efficient, allowing researchers and developers to build and experiment with various models.|Here is another description: Detectron2 is a software framework developed by Facebook AI Research for object detection and segmentation tasks. It is an evolution of the original Detectron framework, offering improved performance and additional features."},
{"detectron2__used_with__a_resnet_50_backbone": "The phrase \"used with\" indicates a combination or integration of two components. In this context, it refers to the utilization of Detectron2 in conjunction with a specific type of neural network architecture known as a ResNet-50 backbone."},
{"a_resnet_50_backbone": "A ResNet-50 backbone is a type of convolutional neural network architecture that serves as the foundational component for many deep learning models. It consists of 50 layers and is known for its efficiency and effectiveness in various computer vision tasks."},
