{"segmentation_errors_from_localization_and_classification_errors": "Segmentation errors from localization and classification errors refer to the mistakes made by instance segmentation models in correctly identifying and outlining the boundaries of objects, as well as correctly categorizing those objects. These errors are distinct from each other and can be more easily analyzed when ground truth boxes are used."},
{"mask_r_cnn__predicts__blobby_masks_with_significant_visual_defects_for_larger_objects": "The predicate \"predicts\" in this context refers to the action of the Mask R-CNN model generating outputs based on input images. Specifically, it indicates the model's capability to produce segmentation masks for detected objects within an image."},
{"blobby_masks_with_significant_visual_defects_for_larger_objects": "Blobby masks with significant visual defects for larger objects refer to the segmentation masks produced by the Mask R-CNN model. These masks tend to have irregular, amorphous shapes and noticeable imperfections, particularly when the objects being segmented are large in size."},
{"mask_ap__is_larger_for__larger_objects_mask_ap_l": "The phrase \"is larger for\" indicates a comparative relationship where the Mask AP metric shows a higher value or better performance when applied to a specific category of objects, in this case, larger objects."},
