{"larger_objects_boundary_ap_l": "\"Larger objects\" in this context refers to objects within an image that have a greater physical size or occupy more pixels. These objects are typically more challenging for object detection models to accurately delineate, especially when the model is prone to predicting blobby masks with significant visual defects."},
