{"general_evaluation_metric": "A general evaluation metric is a standard measure used to assess the performance of a system or model across various tasks. In the context of instance segmentation, it serves as a comprehensive tool to evaluate how well a model performs in different aspects of the task."},
{"general_evaluation_metric__should_track__improvements_in_all_aspects_of_the_task_including_segmentation_categorization_and_localizations": "The phrase \"should track\" indicates a requirement or expectation that the general evaluation metric must monitor or follow the progress or changes in certain areas. In this context, it means the metric needs to observe and record the advancements or enhancements in the model's performance."},
