{"mask_iou": "Mask IoU is a metric used to evaluate the performance of object detection and image segmentation models by measuring the overlap between predicted masks and ground truth masks. It calculates the intersection over union (IoU) of the pixel-wise overlap, providing a measure of similarity and accuracy in segmentation tasks. This metric is scale-invariant, sensitive to object size, and is crucial for calculating evaluation metrics like Average Precision (AP) and Panoptic Quality (PQ).|Here is another description: Mask IoU, or Intersection over Union for masks, is a metric that measures the overlap between the predicted object mask and the ground truth mask. It is a critical indicator of how accurately a model can segment objects, with higher IoU values indicating better segmentation performance. Mask IoU is sensitive to the size of the objects, showing more significant discrepancies for larger objects."},
