{"research_directions__improve__other_error_types": "The predicate \"improve\" in this context signifies the action of making something better or more effective. It implies a process of enhancement or advancement that leads to greater efficiency, accuracy, or overall performance in addressing the specified issue, which in this case is the resolution of different types of errors."},
{"other_error_types": "Other error types represent the various categories or forms of errors that can occur within a given system, process, or field of study. These errors may differ in nature, cause, and impact, requiring distinct approaches for identification, analysis, and resolution. Improving these error types involves developing methods or techniques that can effectively address and reduce their occurrence or severity."},
{"progress__is__harder_to_quantify": "The predicate \"is\" serves as a linking verb that connects the subject \"progress\" with its characteristic or state, which in this case is \"harder to quantify.\" It indicates that the nature of progress in certain research directions is such that it is more difficult to measure or assess."},
{"harder_to_quantify": "\"Harder to quantify\" describes a state where the measurement or assessment of progress is more challenging. In the context of research, this could mean that improvements in certain error types are not as easily measurable or observable as others, making it difficult to track or evaluate the advancement in those specific areas."},
