{"boundary_based_segmentation_measures": "Boundary-based segmentation measures are methods used to assess the performance of image segmentation algorithms by focusing on the alignment of contours between predicted and ground truth masks.|Here is another description: Boundary-based segmentation measures are methods used to assess the quality of image segmentation by focusing on the alignment of contours. They specifically analyze the pixels that are directly on the contours of the masks or in their immediate vicinity.|Here is another description: Boundary-based segmentation measures are methods used to assess the quality of image segmentation by focusing on the alignment of contours between predicted and ground truth masks."},
