{"comparable_pixel_errors_across_object_scales": "Comparable pixel errors across object scales refer to a situation where the errors in pixel predictions are consistent regardless of the size of the objects being segmented. This means that the segmentation errors do not significantly vary whether the objects are small or large."},
{"trimap_iou__calculates_iou_only_for__pixels_around_the_contour": "The predicate \"calculates IoU only for\" indicates that Trimap IoU specifically evaluates the Intersection over Union metric within a limited area. This area is defined as the pixels within a certain distance from the contour of the ground truth mask, distinguishing it from other IoU calculations that may consider the entire mask."},
