{"a_different_score": "The resulting numerical value that differs when the prediction and ground truth masks are swapped, indicating a non-symmetric property in the evaluation metric."},
{"this_asymmetry": "The asymmetry refers to the non-symmetric nature of the Trimap IoU metric, which computes IoU for a region around the ground truth boundary only. This characteristic means that swapping the prediction and ground truth masks will yield different scores."},
{"this_asymmetry__favors__predictions_that_are_larger_than_ground_truth_masks": "The term \"favors\" indicates a bias or preference in the Trimap IoU metric towards certain types of predictions. In this context, it suggests that the metric tends to give better scores to predictions that exhibit specific characteristics compared to others."},
{"predictions_that_are_larger_than_ground_truth_masks": "Predictions that are larger than ground truth masks are those where the predicted area exceeds the actual area defined by the ground truth mask. These types of predictions are preferred by the Trimap IoU metric due to its asymmetric nature, as highlighted in the context."},
{"for_larger_dilated_pseudo_predictions": "For larger (dilated) pseudo-predictions refers to predictions that are expanded or enlarged beyond the actual ground truth boundary. These predictions are tested to see how they affect the Trimap IoU score."},
{"for_larger_dilated_pseudo_predictions__trimap_iou_does_not_drop_below__some_positive_value_irrespective_of_the_error_severity": "Trimap IoU does not drop below indicates that despite the severity of the error in the prediction, the Trimap IoU score remains above a certain threshold. This suggests a resilience or robustness of the Trimap IoU metric under certain conditions."},
{"some_positive_value_irrespective_of_the_error_severity": "Some positive value irrespective of the error severity refers to a minimum threshold that the Trimap IoU score will not fall below, no matter how severe the error in the prediction is. This value is positive, meaning it is greater than zero, and it represents a baseline performance level of the Trimap IoU metric."},
{"for_smaller_eroded_pseudo_predictions": "For smaller (eroded) pseudo-predictions refer to predictions that have been reduced in size, typically through a process of erosion which removes pixels from the boundary of the predicted mask, making it smaller than the actual ground truth mask."},
{"for_smaller_eroded_pseudo_predictions__it_drops_to__0": "The phrase \"it drops to\" indicates a decrease in a measured value, in this case, the Trimap IoU score, as a result of the size reduction of the pseudo-predictions."},
{"0": "The value 0 represents the lowest possible score for Trimap IoU, indicating that there is no overlap between the eroded pseudo-prediction and the region around the ground truth boundary, resulting in a complete failure of the prediction to match the expected output."},
{"the_measure": "The measure refers to the Trimap IoU metric, which evaluates the intersection over union for a region around the ground truth boundary, independent of the prediction.|Here is another description: The measure refers to a method or metric used to evaluate the performance of predictions in comparison to ground truth masks, specifically in the context of image segmentation tasks."},
