{"f_measure__matches__pixels_of_the_predicted_and_ground_truth_contours": "The predicate'matches' in this context signifies that the F-Measure evaluates the alignment of predicted contours with ground truth contours by checking if they fall within a specified distance threshold. This evaluation method allows for some tolerance in contour misalignments, which can be due to inherent ambiguities in the data."},
{"pixels_of_the_predicted_and_ground_truth_contours": "The pixels of the predicted and ground truth contours represent the specific points in an image that are being compared by the F-Measure. The predicted contours are generated by the segmentation algorithm, while the ground truth contours are the correct, manually annotated contours used as a reference for evaluation."},
{"robustness_to_ambiguity": "Robustness to ambiguity refers to the ability of a system or metric to handle and perform well under conditions where there is uncertainty or multiple interpretations of the data. In the context of evaluating contour predictions, it means the metric should not be overly sensitive to small variations or misalignments that could be due to inherent ambiguities in the data."},
