{"nearly_discontinuous": "\"Nearly discontinuous\" describes a characteristic of the F-measure where it can exhibit abrupt changes in value. Specifically, the F-measure can rapidly transition from a perfect score of 1 to a score of 0 with only a slight change in error severity, leading to high variance in task metrics."},
{"f_measure__steps__rapidly_from_1_to_0_when_the_error_severity_changes_by_a_small_amount": "The predicate \"steps\" describes the behavior of the F-measure as it changes in response to variations in error severity. Specifically, it indicates a sudden and significant change in the F-measure value."},
