{"sharp_response_curves__can_lead_to__task_metrics_with_high_variance": "The phrase \"can lead to\" describes a causal relationship where sharp response curves in performance metrics result in certain outcomes. In this context, it suggests that the steep changes in metric values due to small input variations cause a specific effect on the task metrics."},
{"task_metrics_with_high_variance": "Task metrics with high variance are performance indicators that show significant fluctuations in their values. In the context of evaluation metrics like F-measure, high variance means that the metric can change drastically with minor changes in the input, leading to inconsistent and unreliable performance assessments."},
