{"boundary_iou__does_not_evaluate__mask_pixels_further_than_d_pixels_away_from_the_corresponding_ground_truth_or_prediction_boundary": "The predicate \"does not evaluate\" indicates that Boundary IoU excludes certain elements from its assessment. Specifically, it does not consider mask pixels that are located beyond a specified distance (_d_ pixels) from the boundary of either the ground truth or the prediction."},
{"mask_pixels_further_than_d_pixels_away_from_the_corresponding_ground_truth_or_prediction_boundary": "Mask pixels further than _d_ pixels away from the corresponding ground truth or prediction boundary are those pixels in the segmentation mask that are not close enough to the boundary to be included in the Boundary IoU calculation. These pixels are disregarded in the evaluation process."},
