{"a_disc_shaped_mask_and_a_ring_shaped_mask_with_the_same_center_and_outer_radius_plus_an_inner_radius_exactly_d_pixels_smaller": "A disc-shaped mask and a ring-shaped mask with the same center and outer radius, plus an inner radius exactly _d_ pixels smaller, represent a specific scenario where Boundary IoU can yield a perfect score. In this case, despite the masks being non-identical, all non-matching pixels of the disc-shaped mask are further than _d_ pixels away from its boundary, leading to a perfect Boundary IoU score."},
