{"96_5_98_9_95_7_95_0": "The values 96.5, 98.9, 95.7, and 95.0 are specific performance metrics for Mask AP, indicating the accuracy of mask predictions in various scenarios or datasets, showcasing the model's capability in different contexts."},
{"boundary_ap__has_values__85_9_98_9_93_0_73_0": "The predicate \"has_values\" indicates that the subject, Boundary AP, is associated with a set of numerical values. This relation suggests that Boundary AP is quantified or measured using these specific numbers."},
{"85_9_98_9_93_0_73_0": "The object \"85.9, 98.9, 93.0, 73.0\" represents a set of numerical values assigned to the Boundary AP. These values likely reflect different measurements or performance metrics associated with Boundary AP, indicating variability or multiple assessments."},
{"boundary_ap__and__mask_ap": "The 'and' predicate here signifies the conjunction of two metrics, Boundary AP and Mask AP, which are both used to assess different aspects of object detection performance in the COCO dataset."},
{"boundary_ap_and_mask_ap": "Boundary AP and Mask AP are metrics used to evaluate the performance of object detection and segmentation models. They measure the accuracy of the predicted boundaries and masks of objects in an image."},
{"boundary_ap_and_mask_ap__on__coco_val_set": "The predicate 'on' indicates that the metrics Boundary AP and Mask AP are being evaluated specifically on the COCO val set. This means that the performance of the models is being assessed using the validation dataset from the COCO (Common Objects in Context) benchmark."},
{"coco_val_set": "The COCO val set is a subset of the COCO dataset used for validating the performance of computer vision models. It contains a diverse range of images with various objects and scenes, making it a standard benchmark for evaluating object detection and segmentation algorithms.|Here is another description: The COCO val set is a validation dataset from the COCO (Common Objects in Context) dataset, which is widely used for training and evaluating object detection and segmentation algorithms. It contains a variety of images with annotations for objects, allowing for the assessment of model performance."},
{"synthetic_28_28_predictions": "Synthetic 28 \u00d7 28 predictions refer to artificially created data points or outcomes that are 28 units by 28 units in dimension. These predictions are likely used in a machine learning or computer vision context to evaluate or train models."},
