{"mask_ap_l": "Mask AP _L_ is a metric used to evaluate the performance of object detection models, specifically focusing on the accuracy of mask predictions for large objects."},
{"mask_ap_l__does_not_capture__lack_of_fidelity_in_the_synthetic_prediction_for_large_objects": "The predicate \"does not capture\" indicates that Mask AP _L_ fails to accurately reflect or measure a particular aspect or issue related to the object detection task."},
{"lack_of_fidelity_in_the_synthetic_prediction_for_large_objects": "The lack of fidelity in the synthetic prediction for large objects refers to the inaccuracy or poor quality of the predicted masks generated by the model for large objects, which Mask AP _L_ is unable to effectively measure or reflect.|Here is another description: The lack of fidelity in the synthetic prediction for large objects refers to the inaccuracy or poor quality of predictions made by a synthetic model when dealing with large objects, which Boundary AP _L_ is able to detect and measure."},
