{"large_objects__have__area_96_2": "The predicate \"have\" in this context signifies the possession or inclusion of a certain characteristic or attribute. Here, it indicates that large objects possess or are characterized by a specific area size."},
{"area_96_2": "The object \"area _>_ 96 [2]\" describes a specific attribute of the large objects, indicating that their area is greater than 96 squared units. This measurement is used to classify objects as large within the COCO dataset."},
{"synthetic_predictions__allow__us_to_assess_the_segmentation_quality_aspect_in_isolation": "The predicate \"allow\" signifies the capability or permission granted by synthetic predictions to perform a certain action or evaluation. Here, it indicates that synthetic predictions enable a focused assessment of segmentation quality."},
{"us_to_assess_the_segmentation_quality_aspect_in_isolation": "The segmentation quality aspect in isolation refers to evaluating the accuracy and effectiveness of the segmentation process without considering other elements of the instance segmentation task. This isolated assessment helps in understanding the pure performance of the segmentation component."},
{"real_instance_segmentation_models": "Real instance segmentation models refer to actual, operational models used for segmenting instances within images, as opposed to synthetic or simulated models. These models are designed to accurately delineate and classify objects within an image, providing practical applications in various fields such as computer vision, robotics, and autonomous systems."},
{"real_instance_segmentation_models__provide__insights_into_the_ability_of_boundary_ap_to_track_all_aspects_of_the_instance_segmentation_task": "The predicate \"provide\" in this context signifies the action of offering or supplying something valuable or necessary. Here, it indicates that real instance segmentation models are capable of delivering or furnishing certain benefits or information, specifically related to evaluating the performance of Boundary AP in the context of instance segmentation tasks."},
{"insights_into_the_ability_of_boundary_ap_to_track_all_aspects_of_the_instance_segmentation_task": "Insights into the ability of Boundary AP to track all aspects of the instance segmentation task refer to the understanding and knowledge gained about how effectively Boundary AP can monitor and evaluate the comprehensive performance of instance segmentation. This includes assessing not only the accuracy of segmentation but also other critical factors such as the model's robustness, efficiency, and adaptability to different scenarios within the task."},
{"mask_ap__is_compared_with__boundary_ap": "The comparison between Mask AP and Boundary AP involves evaluating and contrasting their effectiveness and accuracy in the context of instance segmentation tasks using datasets like COCO, Cityscapes, and LVIS."},
