{"further_study_boundary_ap": "Boundary AP, or Boundary Average Precision, is a metric used to evaluate the performance of object detection models in terms of their ability to accurately delineate the boundaries of objects within an image. It is a critical measure for assessing the localization accuracy of detected objects."},
{"segmentation_quality__is_isolated_from__categorization_and_localization_errors": "The phrase \"is isolated from\" indicates a methodological approach where the influence of certain factors is minimized or removed to focus on a specific aspect. In this case, segmentation quality is being analyzed independently of other potential sources of error, such as categorization and localization mistakes."},
