{"ground_truth_boxes": "Ground truth boxes refer to the pre-defined, accurate bounding boxes used as a benchmark in object detection and segmentation tasks. They represent the true locations of objects within an image, serving as a standard to evaluate the performance of various algorithms.|Here is another description: Ground truth boxes refer to the accurately labeled and positioned bounding boxes in a dataset used for training and evaluating object detection models. These boxes represent the true locations and extents of objects within images.|Here is another description: The object, \"ground truth boxes,\" represents the accurate bounding boxes that are used as input to the models. These boxes help in disentangling segmentation errors from localization and classification errors during the evaluation.|Here is another description: Ground truth boxes are precise, predefined bounding boxes that accurately delineate the objects within an image. They serve as a benchmark for evaluating the performance of segmentation models."},
{"ground_truth_boxes__are_supplied_to__these_methods": "The phrase \"are supplied to\" indicates the action of providing or feeding ground truth boxes into certain methods or algorithms. This process is crucial for assessing how well these methods can perform when given perfect localization information, thereby isolating other factors like categorization errors."},
